blocks.en:
We study five representative linear ViT variants:
ELU and ReLU ( Katharopoulos et al., 2020 ) , which instantiate ϕ \phi as ELU ⁡ ( ⋅ ) + 1 \mathrm{ELU}(\cdot)+1 and ReLU ⁡ ( ⋅ ) \mathrm{ReLU}(\cdot) , respectively;
InLine ( Han et al., 2024 ) , which uses an identity kernel with subtraction-based normalization;
MHLA ( Zhang et al., 2026 ) , which restores the expressivity of linear attention through token-level multi-head computation with auxiliary convolutions;
and TTT ( Han et al., 2026b ) , which replaces the attention computation entirely with a compact linear-complexity inner model constructed from KV pairs.
The first three variants are drop-in linear operators whose weight shapes exactly match the Softmax attention, while MHLA and TTT introduce additional components.
Full descriptions of different linear ViTs and the corresponding attention operators are given in Section B.1 .

